tags: event

= Staal Resigns!

DuFour is beyond furious that Staal—head of the Commonwealth Army and the man who repeatedly assured the President of the army's power to crush any threat from the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>—has now capitulated to our demands to lift the ban on the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

With his faith in the Commonwealth Army shattered, he has turned back to his old allies among the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span>. And with the bar set so low, perhaps this is a blessing to us. Though they remain our enemies, as they were in the days of normalcy, whoever DuFour selects now is likely to be preferable to Staal’s continued hold on office. And there is this besides: the quiet road Staal had been laying—toward an orderly realm and a settlement with the powers to the north—loses, with him, the one man patient and credible enough to walk it. Whatever he was steering the Commonwealth toward, it will not arrive on his schedule now.

- @treviranus

@treviranus
title: Edgar Westmore -[? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical":&nbsp;Former?] <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>
subtitle: DuFour's preferred choice once again, and [? if traditionalist_leader != "Westmore":former?] <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> party leader.
face-image: img/portraits/Treviranus.jpg
on-arrival: {!
Q.chancellor = "Trevannon";
Q.staal_approval -= 4;

if (Q.traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" && !Q.kvp_formed) {
    Q.treviranus_party = "GNU";
} else if (Q.traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" && Q.kvp_formed) {
    Q.treviranus_party = "CPP";
} else if (Q.traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") {
    Q.treviranus_party = "Traditionalist";
}

Q.chancellor_party = Q.treviranus_party;

Q.staal_marcher_r -= 3;
Q.staal_marcher_influence -= 4;
Q.staal_marcher_support -= 5;
!}

Westmore, despite being once again begged by an older and increasingly sick DuFour, has declined the offer. Instead, he recommends the appointment of rising star and <span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservative</span> leader Godwin Trevannon. With deep ties to Commonwealth industry, the Right, and a pseudo-<span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> veneer, Trevannon is a candidate aimed at stabilizing the Commonwealth’s worsening crisis.

Much like Goodryke’s dismissal in favor of Staal, the political class breathes yet another sigh of relief. Even within the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, many find it easier to confront the devil they know rather than face Staal’s dynamic and unpredictable rule.

Trevannon will seek to construct a working majority via parliament.